 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Interactive problem modelled as a deterministic transcript. A simulated server holds secret (4 digits, leading zeros allowed) and answers a 4-digit guess with the number of positions where guess and secret agree. Return every guess the following strategy makes, in order. Phase 1: for d = 0, 1, ... stop when the known digit counts already sum to 4; for d = 9 infer its count without a guess; otherwise guess dddd to learn the count of d, and stop at once if the answer is 4. Phase 2: let f be the smallest digit with count 0. For each position p = 0..3, with D the ascending distinct digits still unplaced: if D has one digit it is at p; else for each d in D except the last, guess the string with d at p and f elsewhere, and if the answer is 1 place d at p; if no guess hits, place the last. Phase 3: guess the secret itself (answer 4) unless the last guess already was.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk06-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
    "sha256": "9b45427ee65a0467344aa6db91e9b0ff0426a40d4670db3973ca60de4d6eaf26",
    "selector": "/problems/8/inferred_spec"
   }
  ]
 },
